<p>To <dfn export>decompress an archive</dfn> given |inputPath| (a file system path), |outputPath| (a file system path), and optional |options|:</p>

<ol class=algorithm>
  <li>Let |inputFile| be the result of opening |inputPath| for reading.
    If |inputFile| is null, [=throw=] an error.</li>

  <li>Let |inputSize| be the size of |inputFile| in bytes.</li>

  <li>Identify the archive type:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |header| be the first 8 bytes of |inputFile|.</li>

      <li>If |header| starts with [=const/ENCRYPTED_HEADER_MAGIC=]:
        <ol>
          <li>Let |decryptedArchive| be the result of [=decrypting an encrypted archive=] given |inputFile|.
            If decryption fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>
          <li>Set |inputFile| to |decryptedArchive|.</li>
        </ol>
      </li>

      <li>Otherwise, if |header| does not start with [=const/HEADER_MAGIC=]:
        <ol>
          <li>[=throw=] an error ("invalid archive format").</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Locate the footer:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |maxFooterSize| be 65,543 (maximum footer size including magic and size copy).</li>
      <li>Let |readSize| be min(|inputSize|, |maxFooterSize|).</li>

      <li>Seek to position |inputSize| - |readSize| in |inputFile|.</li>
      <li>Let |trailer| be the result of reading |readSize| bytes from |inputFile|.</li>

      <li>Let |footerMagicOffset| be the index of [=const/FOOTER_MAGIC=] within |trailer|, searching from the end.
        If |footerMagicOffset| is not found, [=throw=] an error ("footer not found").</li>

      <li>Let |footerOffset| be |inputSize| - |readSize| + |footerMagicOffset|.</li>

      <li>Seek to position |footerOffset| + 6 (after [=archive/footer_magic=]) in |inputFile|.</li>
      <li>Let |footerSize| be the result of reading a u16le from |inputFile|.</li>

      <li>Seek to position |footerOffset| + 6 + 2 + |footerSize| in |inputFile|.</li>
      <li>Let |footerSizeCopy| be the result of reading a u16le from |inputFile|.</li>

      <li>If |footerSize| is not equal to |footerSizeCopy|:
        <ol>
          <li>[=throw=] an error ("footer size mismatch").</li>
        </ol>
      </li>

      <li>Let |footerStart| be |footerOffset| + 6.</li>
      <li>Let |footerEnd| be |footerStart| + |footerSize|.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Parse the footer:
    <ol>
      <li>Seek to position |footerStart| in |inputFile|.</li>

      <li>Let |sizeHint| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>
      <li>Let |metadataBackwardOffset| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>

      <li>Let |lastMetadataOffset| be |footerStart| - |metadataBackwardOffset|.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Read metadata blocks:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |allMetadata| be an empty list.</li>
      <li>Let |currentMetadataOffset| be |lastMetadataOffset|.</li>

      <li>While |currentMetadataOffset| is greater than the position after [=archive/header_magic=]:
        <ol>
          <li>Seek to position |currentMetadataOffset| in |inputFile|.</li>

          <li>Let |blockType| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.
            If |blockType| is not in the range [10<sub>16</sub>, 1F<sub>16</sub>], [=throw=] an error ("invalid metadata block").</li>

          <li>Let |blockSize| be the result of reading the size field for |blockType| (u8, u16le, u32le, or u64le based on |blockType| % 4).</li>

          <li>Let |blockData| be the result of reading |blockSize| bytes from |inputFile|.</li>

          <li>Let |metadataBlock| be the result of [=parsing a metadata block=] from |blockData| with |blockType|.
            If parsing fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>

          <li>Prepend |metadataBlock| to |allMetadata|.</li>

          <li>Let |previousMetadataOffset| be |metadataBlock|.[=meta/previous_metadata_offset=].</li>
          <li>If |previousMetadataOffset| is 0:
            <ol>
              <li>Set |currentMetadataOffset| to 0.</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
          <li>Otherwise:
            <ol>
              <li>Set |currentMetadataOffset| to |currentMetadataOffset| - |previousMetadataOffset|.</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>If |allMetadata| is empty:
    <ol>
      <li>Handle single-file archive (no metadata):
        <ol>
        <li>Seek to position after [=archive/header_magic=] in |inputFile|.</li>

        <li>Let |outputFile| be the result of opening |outputPath| for writing.
          If |outputFile| is null, [=throw=] an error.</li>

        <li>Let |fileOffset| be the current position in |inputFile|.</li>

        <li>While |fileOffset| is less than |footerStart|:
          <ol>
            <li>Let |blockType| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>

            <li>If |blockType| is in the range [20<sub>16</sub>, 3F<sub>16</sub>]:
              <ol>
                <li>Let |decompressedData| be the result of [=decompressing a compressed block=] given |inputFile|, |blockType|, and |options|.
                  If decompression fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>
                <li>Write |decompressedData| to |outputFile|.</li>
              </ol>
            </li>
            <li>Else if |blockType| is in the range [40<sub>16</sub>, 47<sub>16</sub>]:
              <ol>
                <li>Let |decompressedData| be the result of [=decompressing an uncompressed block=] given |inputFile|, |blockType|, and |options|.
                  If decompression fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>
                <li>Write |decompressedData| to |outputFile|.</li>
              </ol>
            </li>
            <li>Else if |blockType| is in the range [0<sub>16</sub>, 3<sub>16</sub>]:
              <ol>
                <li>Let |blockSize| be the result of reading the size field for |blockType|.</li>
                <li>Skip |blockSize| + 1 bytes in |inputFile| (including padding).</li>
              </ol>
            </li>
            <li>Otherwise:
              <ol>
                <li>[=throw=] an error ("unexpected block type").</li>
              </ol>
            </li>

            <li>Set |fileOffset| to the current position in |inputFile|.</li>
          </ol>
        </li>
        </ol>

        <li>Close |outputFile|.</li>
        <li>Return success.</li>
      </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Handle multi-file archive (with metadata):
    <ol>
      <li>For each |metadataBlock| in |allMetadata|:
        <ol>
          <li>For each |entry| in |metadataBlock|.[=meta/entries=]:
            <ol>
              <li>Let |entryIndex| be the index of |entry| within |metadataBlock|.[=meta/entries=].</li>
              <li>Let |entryName| be |entry|.[=meta/entry_name=].</li>

              <li>If |entryIndex| is less than or equal to |metadataBlock|.[=meta/num_directories=]:
                <ol>
                  <li>Let |dirPath| be |outputPath| joined with |entryName| using the appropriate path separator for the platform.</li>
                  <li>Create the directory at |dirPath| if it does not exist.
                    If directory creation fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>
                </ol>
              </li>
              <li>Otherwise:
                <ol>
                  <li>Let |fileIndex| be |entryIndex| - |metadataBlock|.[=meta/num_directories=] - 1.</li>
                  <li>Let |fileParam| be |metadataBlock|.[=meta/file_params=][|fileIndex|].</li>

                  <li>Let |filePath| be |outputPath| joined with |entryName| using the appropriate path separator for the platform.</li>

                  <li>Let |contentBlockOffset| be |metadataBlock| offset from the beginning of |inputFile| minus |fileParam|.[=meta/file_offset=].</li>

                  <li>Seek to position |contentBlockOffset| in |inputFile|.</li>
                  <li>Let |blockType| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>

                  <li>Let |fileData| be an empty byte sequence.</li>

                  <li>If |blockType| is in the range [20<sub>16</sub>, 3F<sub>16</sub>]:
                    <ol>
                      <li>Let |fileData| be the result of [=decompressing a compressed block=] given |inputFile|, |blockType|, and |options|.
                        If decompression fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>
                    </ol>
                  </li>
                  <li>Else if |blockType| is in the range [40<sub>16</sub>, 47<sub>16</sub>]:
                    <ol>
                      <li>Let |fileData| be the result of [=decompressing an uncompressed block=] given |inputFile|, |blockType|, and |options|.
                        If decompression fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>
                    </ol>
                  </li>
                  <li>Otherwise:
                    <ol>
                      <li>[=throw=] an error ("invalid content block type").</li>
                    </ol>
                  </li>

                  <li>Let |outputFile| be the result of opening |filePath| for writing.
                    If |outputFile| is null, [=throw=] an error.</li>

                  <li>Write |fileData| to |outputFile|.</li>
                  <li>Close |outputFile|.</li>
                </ol>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </ol>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Close |inputFile|.</li>
  <li>Return success.</li>
</ol>

<p>To <dfn export>parse a metadata block</dfn> from |blockData| with |blockType|:</p>

<ol class=algorithm>
  <li>Let |compressionMethod| be None if |blockType| is in [10<sub>16</sub>, 17<sub>16</sub>], otherwise Zstandard.</li>
  <li>Let |checksumMethod| be None if (|blockType| >> 2) & 1 = 0, otherwise XXH64.</li>
  <li>Let |checksumSize| be 0 if |checksumMethod| is None, otherwise 8.</li>

  <li>Let |decompressedData| be |blockData|.</li>

  <li>If |compressionMethod| is Zstandard:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |originalSizeDelta| be the result of reading a LEB128 from the beginning of |blockData|.
        Let |pos| be the number of bytes consumed.</li>

      <li>Let |compressionParams| be an empty byte sequence.
        While |pos| is less than the length of |blockData| and the byte at |blockData|[|pos|] is not the start of the Zstandard data:
          <ol>
            <li>Append the byte at |blockData|[|pos|] to |compressionParams|.</li>
            <li>Increment |pos| by 1.</li>
          </ol>
        </ol>

      <li>Let |dataStart| be |pos|.</li>
      <li>Let |compressedSize| be the length of |blockData| - |dataStart| - |checksumSize|.</li>
      <li>Let |originalSize| be |compressedSize| + |originalSizeDelta|.</li>

      <li>If |checksumMethod| is XXH64:
        <ol>
          <li>Let |checksumOffset| be |dataStart| + |compressedSize|.</li>
          <li>Let |storedChecksum| be |blockData| from |checksumOffset| to |checksumOffset| + 8.</li>
          <li>Let |computedChecksum| be the XXH64 hash of |blockData| from |dataStart| to |dataStart| + |compressedSize| with seed 0, encoded as u64le.</li>
          <li>If |storedChecksum| is not equal to |computedChecksum|:
            <ol>
              <li>Return failure ("checksum mismatch").</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </li>

      <li>Let |compressedData| be |blockData| from |dataStart| to |dataStart| + |compressedSize|.</li>

      <li>Let |decompressedData| be the result of decompressing |compressedData| using Zstandard [[RFC8878]].
        The decompressed data should be a sequence of Zstandard blocks.
        Process Zstandard blocks consecutively until the final block is signalled, at which point all compressed bytes should have been consumed.
        If decompression fails or the decompressed size is not equal to |originalSize|, return failure ("decompression failed").</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>Otherwise:
    <ol>
      <li>If |checksumMethod| is XXH64:
        <ol>
          <li>Let |dataSize| be the length of |blockData| - 8.</li>
          <li>Let |storedChecksum| be |blockData| from |dataSize| to |dataSize| + 8.</li>
          <li>Let |computedChecksum| be the XXH64 hash of |blockData| from 0 to |dataSize| with seed 0, encoded as u64le.</li>
          <li>If |storedChecksum| is not equal to |computedChecksum|:
            <ol>
              <li>Return failure ("checksum mismatch").</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
          <li>Set |decompressedData| to |blockData| from 0 to |dataSize|.</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Parse |decompressedData| according to the [=metadata block=] structure and return the resulting metadata object.
    If parsing fails, return failure ("invalid metadata").</li>
</ol>

<p>To <dfn export>decompress a compressed block</dfn> given |inputFile|, |blockType|, and |options|:</p>

<ol class=algorithm>
  <li>Let |hasDictionary| be true if (|blockType| >> 5) & 1 = 1, otherwise false.</li>
  <li>Let |transformed| be true if (|blockType| >> 4) & 1 = 1, otherwise false.</li>
  <li>Let |checksumMethod| be None if (|blockType| >> 3) & 1 = 0, otherwise XXH64.</li>
  <li>Let |checksumSize| be 0 if |checksumMethod| is None, otherwise 8.</li>

  <li>Let |transformerIndex| be 0.
  <li>If |transformed| is true:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |transformerIndex| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Let |dictionaryIndex| be 0.
  <li>If |hasDictionary| is true:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |dictionaryIndex| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Let |allChunks| be an empty list.</li>

  <li>While the end of the block has not been reached:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |compressedSize| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>
      <li>Let |originalSizeDelta| be the result of reading a LEB128 from |inputFile|.</li>
      <li>Let |originalSize| be |compressedSize| + |originalSizeDelta|.</li>

      <li>If |originalSize| is greater than |compressedSize|:
        <ol>
          <li>Return failure ("invalid size delta: original size cannot be larger than compressed size").</li>
        </ol>
      </li>

      <li>Let |compressionParams| be an empty byte sequence.
        While the current byte is not the start of the Zstandard data:
          <ol>
            <li>Read a byte from |inputFile| and append it to |compressionParams|.</li>
          </ol>
        </ol>

      <li>Let |compressedData| be the result of reading |compressedSize| bytes from |inputFile|.</li>

      <li>Let |checksum| be an empty byte sequence.
      <li>If |checksumMethod| is XXH64:
        <ol>
          <li>Let |checksum| be the result of reading 8 bytes from |inputFile|.</li>
          <li>Let |computedChecksum| be the XXH64 hash of |compressedData| with seed 0, encoded as u64le.</li>
          <li>If |checksum| is not equal to |computedChecksum|:
            <ol>
              <li>Return failure ("checksum mismatch").</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </li>

      <li>Let |decompressedData| be the result of decompressing |compressedData| using Zstandard [[RFC8878]].
        The compressed data is a sequence of Zstandard blocks.
        Process Zstandard blocks consecutively until the final block is signalled, at which point all compressed bytes should have been consumed.
        If decompression fails or the decompressed size is not equal to |originalSize|, return failure ("decompression failed").</li>

      <li>If |transformed| is true and |options| is provided and |options|["transformer"] is provided:
        <ol>
          <li>Let |transformedData| be the result of applying the transformer specified by |transformerIndex| to |decompressedData| as postprocessing.
            If the transformation fails, return failure ("transformation failed").</li>
          <li>Set |decompressedData| to |transformedData|.</li>
        </ol>
      </li>

      <li>Append |decompressedData| to |allChunks|.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Return the concatenation of all byte sequences in |allChunks|.</li>
</ol>

<p>To <dfn export>decompress an uncompressed block</dfn> given |inputFile|, |blockType|, and |options|:</p>

<ol class=algorithm>
  <li>Let |checksumMethod| be None if (|blockType| >> 2) & 1 = 0, otherwise XXH64.</li>
  <li>Let |checksumSize| be 0 if |checksumMethod| is None, otherwise 8.</li>

  <li>Let |blockSize| be the result of reading the size field for |blockType| (u8, u16le, u32le, or u64le based on |blockType| % 4).</li>

  <li>Let |dataSize| be |blockSize| - |checksumSize|.</li>

  <li>Let |data| be the result of reading |dataSize| bytes from |inputFile|.</li>

  <li>If |checksumMethod| is XXH64:
    <ol>
      <li>Let |checksum| be the result of reading 8 bytes from |inputFile|.</li>
      <li>Let |computedChecksum| be the XXH64 hash of |data| with seed 0, encoded as u64le.</li>
      <li>If |checksum| is not equal to |computedChecksum|:
        <ol>
          <li>Return failure ("checksum mismatch").</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Skip the padding byte if present (if the total block size including the padding byte is odd).</li>

  <li>Return |data|.</li>
</ol>

<p>To <dfn export>decrypt an encrypted archive</dfn> given |inputFile|:</p>

<ol class=algorithm>
  <li>Let |encryptedHeaderMagic| be the result of reading 8 bytes from |inputFile|.
    If |encryptedHeaderMagic| is not equal to [=const/ENCRYPTED_HEADER_MAGIC=], return failure ("invalid encrypted header").</li>

  <li>Let |lgWorkFactor| be the result of reading 1 byte from |inputFile|.</li>
  <li>If |lgWorkFactor| is not in the range [0C<sub>16</sub>, 3F<sub>16</sub>), return failure ("invalid work factor").</li>

  <li>Let |scryptEphemeralSecret| be the result of reading 16 bytes from |inputFile|.</li>
  <li>Let |encryptedFileKey| be the result of reading 32 bytes from |inputFile|.</li>
  <li>Let |ageHeaderMac| be the result of reading 32 bytes from |inputFile|.</li>

  <li>Let |payload| be the remaining bytes in |inputFile|.</li>

  <li>Construct the AGE v1 header:
    <pre>
age-encryption.org/v1
-> scrypt <var>scryptEphemeralSecretBase64</var> <var>lgWorkFactorDecimal</var>
<var>encryptedFileKeyBase64</var>
--- <var>ageHeaderMacBase64</var>
    </pre>
    Where:
    <ul>
      <li>|scryptEphemeralSecretBase64| is the base64 encoding of |scryptEphemeralSecret| without padding.</li>
      <li>|lgWorkFactorDecimal| is the decimal representation of |lgWorkFactor|.</li>
      <li>|encryptedFileKeyBase64| is the base64 encoding of |encryptedFileKey| without padding.</li>
      <li>|ageHeaderMacBase64| is the base64 encoding of |ageHeaderMac| without padding.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li>Prompt the user for the decryption passphrase.</li>

  <li>Let |decryptedPayload| be the result of decrypting |payload| using the AGE v1 format [[AGE]] with the provided passphrase.
    If decryption fails, return failure ("decryption failed").</li>

  <li>Verify that |decryptedPayload| is a valid unencrypted archive:
    <ol>
      <li>If |decryptedPayload| does not start with [=const/HEADER_MAGIC=], return failure ("invalid decrypted archive").</li>
      <li>If |decryptedPayload| does not contain a [=archive/size_hint_block=], return failure ("missing size hint block").</li>
      <li>If |decryptedPayload| contains any spacer blocks, return failure ("unexpected spacer block").</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Return |decryptedPayload| as a byte sequence.</li>
</ol>
-->

<!-- Obsolete draft, superseded by formula blocks:
<p>A <dfn>transformer</dfn> is a WebAssembly module that performs preprocessing on data before compression and postprocessing after decompression.
Transformers are identified by a 1-based index within the metadata block.</p>

<p>Transformers are stored in [=transformer blocks=] and can be referenced by [=compressed blocks=] and [=file parameters=].</p>

<p>To <dfn export>apply a transformer</dfn> given |transformerModule| (a WebAssembly module), |inputData| (a byte sequence), and |mode| ("preprocess" or "postprocess"):</p>

<ol class=algorithm>
  <li>Let |instance| be the result of instantiating |transformerModule| as a WebAssembly module.
    If instantiation fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>

  <li>If |instance| does not export an exported function named "transform":
    <ol>
      <li>[=throw=] an error ("transformer missing required export").</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Let |transformFunction| be the exported "transform" function from |instance|.</li>

  <li>Let |memory| be the exported memory from |instance|, if any.
    Otherwise, let |memory| be the default WebAssembly memory.</li>

  <li>Let |inputOffset| be the result of allocating |inputData|.[=length=] bytes in |memory|.
    If allocation fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>

  <li>Copy |inputData| into |memory| at offset |inputOffset|.</li>

  <li>Let |modeValue| be 1 if |mode| is "preprocess", otherwise 2 if |mode| is "postprocess".</li>

  <li>Let |result| be the result of invoking |transformFunction| with arguments (|inputOffset|, |inputData|.[=length=], |modeValue|).
    If the invocation fails, [=throw=] an error.</li>

  <li>If |result| is not a WebAssembly integer or is negative:
    <ol>
      <li>[=throw=] an error ("transformer returned invalid result").</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Let |outputOffset| be |result|.</li>

  <li>If |instance| exports an exported function named "get_output_size":
    <ol>
      <li>Let |getOutputSizeFunction| be the exported "get_output_size" function from |instance|.</li>
      <li>Let |outputSize| be the result of invoking |getOutputSizeFunction| with no arguments.</li>
      <li>If |outputSize| is not a WebAssembly integer or is negative:
        <ol>
          <li>[=throw=] an error ("transformer returned invalid output size").</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>Otherwise:
    <ol>
      <li>[=throw=] an error ("transformer missing get_output_size export").</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Let |outputData| be the result of reading |outputSize| bytes from |memory| at offset |outputOffset|.</li>

  <li>If |instance| exports an exported function named "cleanup":
    <ol>
      <li>Let |cleanupFunction| be the exported "cleanup" function from |instance|.</li>
      <li>Invoke |cleanupFunction| with no arguments. Ignore any errors.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Return |outputData|.</li>
</ol>

<p class=note>Transformers SHOULD be deterministic: the same input with the same mode SHOULD always produce the same output.
Non-deterministic transformers MAY produce different outputs for the same input, but this MAY result in different compressed archives for the same uncompressed data.</p>

<p class=note>Transformers SHOULD NOT have side effects external to the WebAssembly module (such as file system or network access).
Implementations MAY restrict or prohibit such side effects.</p>

<p>To <dfn export>validate a transformer module</dfn> given |transformerModule|:</p>

<ol class=algorithm>
  <li>Let |instance| be the result of instantiating |transformerModule| as a WebAssembly module.
    If instantiation fails, return failure.</li>

  <li>If |instance| does not export an exported function named "transform", return failure.</li>

  <li>If |instance| does not export an exported function named "get_output_size", return failure.</li>

  <li>Return success.</li>
</ol>

<p>The following interface is the expected interface for transformer modules:</p>

<pre class=def>
// Exported functions:
export function transform(input_offset: number, input_size: number, mode: number): number;
// Returns the offset in WebAssembly memory where the output data is written.
// mode: 1 for preprocessing (before compression), 2 for postprocessing (after decompression)

export function get_output_size(): number;
// Returns the size of the output data in bytes.

export function cleanup(): void;
// Optional. Called after transform() to release any resources.

// WebAssembly memory:
export memory: WebAssembly.Memory;
// Optional. If not provided, the default memory is used.
</pre>

<div class=note>
  <p>Transformer execution profile:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Transformers SHOULD execute in O(n) time where n is the input size.</li>
    <li>Transformers SHOULD use O(1) additional memory beyond the input and output buffers.</li>
    <li>Transformers SHOULD complete within a reasonable time frame (e.g., less than 1 second per MB of data on typical hardware).</li>
    <li>Implementations MAY impose resource limits on transformer execution (time, memory, CPU cycles).</li>
  </ul>
</div>
-->

<h2 id=conformance>
Conformance</h2>

<h3 id=extraction>
Extraction</h3>

Writing an [=archive value=] to a file system is outside the archive model.
A decompressor doing so is subject to the following requirements:

* It MUST NOT create, modify or remove any file outside the destination directory,
    including through symbolic links or other redirections already present in the destination.
* It SHOULD map an [=entry name=] whose [=entry name/encoding=] is "`wtf-8`" to the platform's native Unicode name
    (e.g. UTF-16 with lone surrogates on Windows), and
    an [=entry name=] whose [=entry name/encoding=] is "`raw`" to the identical byte sequence where the platform allows.
* If an [=entry name=] can't be represented on the platform or has a special meaning there
    (e.g. a name containing `\` or `:`, or a reserved device name on Windows),
    it MUST either fail or report a substituted name to the user; it MUST NOT silently use a different name.
* If multiple [=entry names=] in a directory map to the same file system name
    (e.g. due to case insensitivity or Unicode normalization),
    it MUST either fail or report the conflict, and MUST NOT write a later entry through an earlier one.
* It MAY ignore any [=file node/extra=] or [=directory node/extra=].
    It SHOULD NOT apply ownership information such as `unix-uid` and `unix-gid` unless explicitly requested.

Issue: Symbolic links and hard links are not part of the archive model yet.

<!--
<p>As well as sections marked as non-normative, all authoring guidelines, diagrams, examples, and notes in this specification are non-normative.
Everything else in this specification is normative.</p>

<p>The key words MAY, MUST, MUST NOT, SHOULD, and SHOULD NOT in this specification are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 [[RFC2119]]
when, and only when, they appear in all capitals, as shown here.</p>

<p>A conforming <dfn>compressor</dfn> MUST implement all algorithms specified in this specification.
Specifically:</p>

<ul>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=compress a file=] algorithm.</li>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=compress a byte sequence=] algorithm.</li>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=apply a transformer=] algorithm for preprocessing.</li>
  <li>It MUST generate valid archives that conform to the syntax specified in the Syntax section.</li>
  <li>It MUST handle [=barely compressible=] data correctly by using uncompressed blocks when compression would not reduce size.</li>
  <li>It MUST generate valid checksums when checksums are enabled.</li>
  <li>It MUST ensure that all constraints specified in the Syntax section are satisfied (e.g., offset ranges, size limits, etc.).</li>
</ul>

<p>A conforming <dfn>decompressor</dfn> MUST implement all algorithms specified in this specification.
Specifically:</p>

<ul>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=decompress an archive=] algorithm.</li>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=parse a metadata block=] algorithm.</li>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=decompress a compressed block=] algorithm.</li>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=decompress an uncompressed block=] algorithm.</li>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=decrypt an encrypted archive=] algorithm if it supports encrypted archives.</li>
  <li>It MUST correctly implement the [=apply a transformer=] algorithm for postprocessing.</li>
  <li>It MUST validate checksums when present and fail on checksum mismatch.</li>
  <li>It MUST validate all constraints specified in the Syntax section and fail on constraint violations.</li>
</ul>

<p>A conforming <dfn>transformer</dfn> (WebAssembly module) MUST implement the required interface:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>It MUST export a function named "transform" that accepts the specified parameters.</li>
  <li>It MUST export a function named "get_output_size" that returns the output size.</li>
  <li>It MUST write output data to WebAssembly memory at the offset returned by "transform".</li>
  <li>It MAY export a function named "cleanup" for resource cleanup.</li>
</ul>

<p class=note>Conformance for transformers is defined at the module interface level.
The actual transformation logic is implementation-dependent and not specified by this standard.</p>

<p>An implementation is not required to support:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Encryption/decryption (encrypted archives).</li>
  <li>Transformer blocks and transformation.</li>
  <li>Dictionary blocks and dictionary-based compression.</li>
  <li>Optional metadata (CBOR-encoded).</li>
  <li>Specific compression levels or Zstandard features beyond the basic frame format.</li>
</ul>

<p>However, if an implementation claims to support any of these optional features, it MUST conform to the relevant algorithms and constraints specified in this specification.</p>

<p>Implementations MAY impose additional restrictions beyond those specified in this specification:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>Maximum file size or archive size limits.</li>
  <li>Maximum number of files or directories in an archive.</li>
  <li>Maximum chunk size or number of chunks.</li>
  <li>Resource limits for transformer execution (time, memory, CPU).</li>
  <li>Restrictions on supported file names, metadata, or path separators.</li>
</ul>

<p>Such restrictions SHOULD be documented and SHOULD NOT prevent processing of valid archives that do not exceed the specified limits.</p>

<p>A conforming implementation MAY:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Reject archives that exceed implementation-defined limits.</li>
  <li>Use optimized or alternative algorithms that produce the same result as the specified algorithms.</li>
  <li>Perform operations in a different order than specified, as long as the result is identical.</li>
  <li>Cache intermediate results for performance.</li>
  <li>Parallelize independent operations (e.g., decompressing multiple chunks concurrently).</li>
</ul>

<p>A conforming implementation MUST NOT:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Accept invalid archives or archives that violate the specified syntax.</li>
  <li>Generate invalid archives or archives that violate the specified syntax.</li>
  <li>Ignore checksums when present.</li>
  <li>Ignore constraint violations (e.g., size limits, offset ranges).</li>
  <li>Fail to process a valid archive that does not exceed implementation-defined limits.</li>
</ul>
-->

